s":345,"closed_issues":2336,"state":"open","created_at":"2026-04-13T15:59:35Z","updated_at":"2026-10-22T08:21:32Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":10,"created_at":"2026-10-06T18:42:31Z","updated_at":"2026-10-07T19:11:22Z","closed_at":"2026-10-07T18:34:32Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124233","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124233","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124233.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124233.patch","merged_at":"2026-10-07T18:34:32Z"},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\nImproves security against offset table rewrites and ROP attacks by enabling `PIE` and `RELRO`.\r\nAs far as I'm aware both have negligible cost and should have been enabled long ago.\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\n- position-independent executable (PIE): unlocks address-space layout randomization (ASLR). This protects against ROP attacks, where attackers can use known code layout to their advantage.\r\n- relocation read-only (RELRO): prevents attackers from overwriting global offset tables, which attackers can use to replace functions with their own malicious code.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users